Title:
ApiHashing — Hash-based x64 replacements for GetModuleHandle/GetProcAddress with EAF-safe reads and API Set resolution

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
ApiHashing is a Windows x64 API hashing library that replaces GetModuleHandleA/W, GetProcAddress, and GetModuleFileNameW using CRC32B hashes and manual resolution via the PEB loader lists and PE export directory. It focuses on resilient API resolution in modern Windows environments, including forwarded exports (by name and ordinal), ordinal-only exports, and api-ms*/ext-ms* API Set contract-to-host DLL mapping across multiple schema versions. A key feature is EAF (Export Address Filtering) bypass support by performing “safe” memory reads through small read gadgets (e.g., `mov rax, [rax]; ret`) scanned from a module’s `.text` section instead of direct dereferences. This is primarily useful for malware developers, red team tool authors, and offensive security researchers building loaders/shellcode that want to avoid static imports and certain user-mode hooks/telemetry patterns. It’s interesting because it combines practical API hashing with robust handling of Windows API Sets and forwarders—common failure points in simplistic hash resolvers.

Technical Focus:
- PEB traversal (InLoadOrderModuleList) for module enumeration
- PE export directory parsing and hashed function lookup (CRC32B)
- Forwarded export handling (name + ordinal) and ordinal resolution
- Windows API Set namespace parsing (api-ms-*, ext-ms-*) and host redirection
- EAF-aware memory access via ROP-style read gadgets from `.text`

Use Cases:
- Building import-less loaders/shellcode that resolve WinAPI dynamically by hash
- Implementing more reliable GetProcAddress-like resolution that supports API Sets and forwarders
- Reducing static indicators (import table strings) in offensive tooling
- Researching/replicating EAF bypass patterns using gadget-based reads
- Creating custom reflective loaders or in-memory execution frameworks on x64 Windows

Keywords:
Windows x64, API hashing, CRC32B, PEB, InLoadOrderModuleList, PE exports, export directory, GetProcAddress replacement, GetModuleHandle replacement, GetModuleFileNameW replacement, forwarded exports, ordinal exports, API Set, api-ms-win, ext-ms-win, ApiSet schema V2 V3 V4 V6, EAF, Export Address Filtering, ROP gadgets, `.text` scanning, libloaderapi